content"><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/dokuwiki/es/index#5"><=
img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.com/dokuwiki.png">Ed=
it in Dokuwiki</a><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/asciidoc/es/i=
ndex#5"><img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.com/asciido=
c32.png">Edit in Asciidoc</a><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/ma=
rkdown/es/index#5"><img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.=
com/markdown.png">Edit in Markdown</a></div></div>=F0=9F=93=A5 Formatos de =
entrada</h2>
<p></p>
PlantUML le permite generar diagramas a partir de varios formatos de entrad=
a de origen:
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/sources">Datos de entrada de origen:=
 <em>C=C3=B3mo y d=C3=B3nde se pueden escribir diagramas</em></a></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
Puede elegir entre diferentes codificaciones internas:
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/text-encoding">Codificaci=C3=B3n de =
texto PlantUML</a></li>
</ul>
<a style=3D"position:relative;top:-38px;" name=3D"6e560fe71abef84f"></a>
<!--heading--><h2 class=3D"chap"><img title=3D"Back to top" src=3D"https://=
plantuml.com/backtop1.svg" width=3D"20" height=3D"20" class=3D"backtop"><di=
v class=3D"dropdown"><button class=3D"dropbtn"><img width=3D"16" height=3D"=
16" src=3D"https://plantuml.com/edit1.svg"></button><div class=3D"dropdown-=
content"><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/dokuwiki/es/index#6"><=
img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.com/dokuwiki.png">Ed=
it in Dokuwiki</a><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/asciidoc/es/i=
ndex#6"><img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.com/asciido=
c32.png">Edit in Asciidoc</a><a href=3D"http://alphadoc.plantuml.com/cmp/ma=
rkdown/es/index#6"><img width=3D"20" height=3D"20" src=3D"https://plantuml.=
com/markdown.png">Edit in Markdown</a></div></div>=E2=9A=99 Layout Engines =
and Options</h2>
<p></p>
PlantUML allows you to use several different <a href=3D"https://plantuml.co=
m/es/layout-engines">layout engines</a>:
<p></p>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/graphviz-dot">Graphviz</a> is the de=
fault engine. Relies on an external program;</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/smetana02">Smetana</a> <em>(Use <cod=
e class=3D"cod">!pragma layout smetana</code> in the file or <code class=3D=
"cod">-Playout=3Dsmetana</code> on the command-line.)</em> is a internal po=
rt of Graphviz to Java. Tends to make slightly straighter arrows;</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/vizjs">VizJs</a> uses JavaScript. <e=
m>(Use <code class=3D"cod">-graphvizdot vizjs</code> on the command line.)<=
/em> Tends to space out nodes more, resulting in a bigger diagram;</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/elk">ELK (Eclipse Layout Kernel)</a>=
. <em>(Use <code class=3D"cod">!pragma layout elk</code>  in the file or <c=
ode class=3D"cod">-Playout=3Delk</code> on the command-line.)</em> Supports=
 only orthogonal layout, and doesn't cover all features.</li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/sequence-diagram">Sequence diagrams</a> =
have 2 engines:
<ul>
<li><em>Puma</em> is the older and still default engine;</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://plantuml.com/es/teoz">Teoz</a> <em>(Use <code class=
=3D"cod">!pragma teoz true</code>  in the file or <code class=3D"cod">-Pteo=
z=3Dtrue</code> on the command-line)</em> is a new engine that has some uni=
que features: <em>anchors (named arrows/messages), duration, nested boxes..=
.</em></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<blockquote>
Achieving good layout with PlantUML is sometimes non-trivial.=20
<em>See <a href=3D"https://isgb.otago.ac.nz/infosci/mark.george/Wiki/wiki/P=
lantUML%20GraphViz%20Layout">PlantUML GraphViz Layout</a> by Mark George at=
 University of Otago for more advice.</em>
</blockquote>
<a style=3D"position:relative;top:-38px;" name=3D"ffc0ab0a7e38b981"></a>
